Subject: [PATCH] q35: reproduce Ubuntu TDX ACPI state in the private qtest tool

Ubuntu's tdx_kvm_init sets eoi_intercept_unsupported before building ACPI.
The offline exporter cannot call KVM. Reproduce that assignment only under
qtest, without changing the table builders or any guest-execution path.
This patch is exclusive to the native release tool, never the deployed QEMU.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Oasis offline release tool]

--- a/hw/i386/pc_q35.c
+++ b/hw/i386/pc_q35.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include "hw/rtc/mc146818rtc.h"
 #include "sysemu/tcg.h"
 #include "sysemu/kvm.h"
+#include "sysemu/qtest.h"
 #include "hw/i386/kvm/clock.h"
 #include "hw/pci-host/q35.h"
 #include "hw/pci/pcie_port.h"
@@ -143,6 +144,11 @@
     bool keep_pci_slot_hpc;
     uint64_t pci_hole64_size = 0;
 
+    /* Mirror tdx_kvm_init's ACPI input without creating a TD. */
+    if (qtest_enabled()) {
+        x86ms->eoi_intercept_unsupported = true;
+    }
+
     /* Check whether RAM fits below 4G (leaving 1/2 GByte for IO memory
      * and 256 Mbytes for PCI Express Enhanced Configuration Access Mapping
      * also known as MMCFG).
